# Code owners
#
# This repository is owned by a personal account, not an organisation, so there are
# no teams. Ownership is by individual handle, and the `require_code_owner_review`
# rule in the "master" ruleset routes reviews here.
#
# The repo-owner line at the bottom catches everything not claimed above. Replace
# the @TEAM-* placeholders as engineers are onboarded; an unclaimed path still
# falls through to @rossigee, so nothing is unreviewed in the meantime.

# Default owner for everything not claimed below.
*                               @rossigee

# --- Authentication and authorization ---------------------------------------
# The three-tier auth model lives here: HTTP Basic for apt clients, OIDC for the
# web UI, bearer tokens for CI. Phase 1 of the v1.0 roadmap rewrites all three.
internal/acl/                   @rossigee
internal/aptauth/               @rossigee
internal/webauth/               @rossigee
internal/config/                @rossigee
internal/apiserver/router.go    @rossigee
internal/apiserver/acl.go       @rossigee

# --- Storage, key layout and snapshots ---------------------------------------
# Phase 2 moves to per-tenant MinIO endpoints and credentials. Pool key layout
# and snapshot format changes are data-loss capable, so these get a second reader.
/internal/repo/                 @rossigee
/internal/storage/              @rossigee
internal/model/                 @rossigee

# --- Rendering and metadata --------------------------------------------------
# Served Packages/Release content. Getting this wrong silently breaks apt clients.
internal/aptmeta/               @rossigee
internal/index/                 @rossigee
internal/reconcile/             @rossigee

# --- UI, templates and CSS ---------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4 replaces all of this with Bootstrap. Also owns accessibility.
internal/templates/             @rossigee
internal/htmlpages/             @rossigee

# --- CI, releases and the image pipeline ------------------------------------
# Release workflow owns version tags; build.yaml must never write them.
/.github/workflows/             @rossigee
Dockerfile                      @rossigee
Makefile                        @rossigee

# --- Documentation -----------------------------------------------------------
docs/                           @rossigee
ROADMAP.md                      @rossigee
SECURITY.md                     @rossigee
AGENTS.md                       @rossigee
